  "configuration_id": "config_036",
  "reason": "Evidence: The current best is config_005 (RNA-only, scvi_n200, multiprofile, avgpool) at 0.650. The only multimodal test (config_030: scvi_n200 + resnet50, avgpool, concat) scored 0.632, slightly *worse* than RNA-only, suggesting the weak resnet50 image encoder (image-only acc=0.208) adds noise. Key uncertainty: is the image modality fundamentally uninformative, or was resnet50 simply too weak to contribute useful signal? This experiment (config_036) pairs the best-validated RNA setup (scvi_n200, multiprofile, avgpool) with the strongest available image encoder (imagenet_vit_l) using the same concat fusion. It directly tests whether a stronger visual encoder can make multimodal fusion competitive with or exceed the RNA-only baseline. If it succeeds, it opens a promising multimodal direction; if it fails, we can confidently abandon multimodal and focus remaining budget on RNA-only refinements. This is the highest-information experiment available because it resolves the single most consequential design question (is multimodal worth pursuing?) with one test, rather than incrementally tuning a direction that already appears suboptimal."
}

